It does not bundle, import, link or modify any training engine. Each adapter
writes a config file and starts the engine's own command line as a separate
process in the engine's own virtualenv. The engines are installed unmodified at
the versions in pins.json, each under its own licence:
  Axolotl                Apache-2.0
  LLaMA-Factory          Apache-2.0
  torchtune              BSD-3-Clause
No engine here is under AGPL or LGPL, even as a separate process. Unsloth was
removed as an engine on 2026-11-15 because its CLI carries AGPL-3.0 headers.
tools/spdx_gate.py fails when any file here imports the Unsloth packages or lists
them as a dependency, or lacks a permissive SPDX header.

GGUF export runs llama.cpp's convert_hf_to_gguf.py and llama-quantize (MIT) as
separate programs when LLAMA_CPP_DIR points at them. They are not bundled.

kit/studio_engine_kit/engines.json and tests/conformance/fixtures/*.json are
copies of the Freeweights Studio contract (Allternit platform repository,
services/studio-spec, Apache-2.0, same owner). kit/studio_engine_kit/spec-sync.json
records the source commit and the sha256 of each copy.

Axolotl, LLaMA-Factory, torchtune, llama.cpp, PyTorch, MLX and NVIDIA
are names of their owners' projects and products. They are used here only to
say which upstream program an adapter starts; no endorsement is implied.
